# Raw cloned documentation repos (huge, third-party, regenerable via
# scripts/download_sources.py) - never push these directly, see
# ATTRIBUTION.md for why the extracted dataset/model are handled
# differently from the raw clones themselves.
data/raw/

# Intermediate raw-text dump (index_documents.py's output) - not
# useful on its own without data/raw/ (which isn't published either),
# and nothing downstream reads it once commands.json exists.
data/processed/documents.json

# Prebuilt RAG index - embeddings.npy alone is ~268MB, over GitHub's
# 100MB hard per-file limit (push would be rejected outright). Cheap
# to regenerate locally: `python scripts/build_index.py` (~25s) from
# the published dataset.jsonl.
data/processed/rag_index/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Training checkpoints - only the final model dirs are meant to be
# published (per ATTRIBUTION.md/LICENSE), not every intermediate
# checkpoint-*/ subfolder saved during training.
models/*/checkpoint-*/

# Local tool/editor state - meaningless outside this machine, no
# reason to publish (session IDs, PIDs, local lock state). NOT the
# whole .claude/ dir - .claude/skills/ holds real, useful project
# documentation (e.g. the UI design system) worth publishing.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/*.lock
.vscode/

# Internal engineering log - detailed working notes (bug-by-bug pipeline
# history, decision rationale), not meant for the public repo. README.md
# and ATTRIBUTION.md stay published (setup instructions + the license
# disclosure the project specifically needs).
01_Project_Overview.md
02_Dataset_Pipeline.md
03_LoRA_Training.md
04_Testing_Results.md
05_Roadmap.md
06_Decisions_Log.md
07_RAG.md
